# Alice, Bob and Carol enroll in robotics, which requires control, safety and algebra.
# Prior learning supplies Carol's control result. Alice and Carol receive certificates;
# Bob lacks safety. Shows recursive requirements, absence of counterexamples,
# multiheaded existential rules and certificates whose witnesses contain dossier witnesses.

Robotics has requirement Control and Robotics has requirement Safety.
Control has prerequisite Algebra.
Alice is an enrollee of Robotics.
Bob is an enrollee of Robotics.
Carol is an enrollee of Robotics.
Alice has completed Control and Alice has completed Algebra and Alice has completed Safety.
Bob has completed Control and Bob has completed Algebra.
Carol has completed Algebra and Carol has completed Safety.
priorLearning(Carol, Control, 90).

# Derive accepted learning before testing which requirements are still missing.
For every S and M and G,
if priorLearning(S, M, G) and G is at least 85 then S has completed M.
For every C and M, if C has requirement M then C has requiredModule M.
For every C and M and P,
if C has requiredModule M and M has prerequisite P then C has requiredModule P.
For every S and C and M,
if S is an enrollee of C and C has requiredModule M
and it is not known that S has completed M
then missing(S, C, M).
For every S and C and M, if missing(S, C, M) then S has incompleteCourse C.
For every S and C,
if S is an enrollee of C and it is not known that S has incompleteCourse C
then S has completedCourse C.

# One firing supplies a dossier and audit entry, sharing their references across heads.
For every S and C,
if S has completedCourse C then there exists D and A such that
D is a dossier and A is an auditEntry and S has dossier D
and D has course C and A is an audit of D.

# A second firing refers to the existing dossier; it does not invent a replacement.
For every S and D and C,
if S is an enrollee of C and S has dossier D and D has course C then there exists K such that
K is a certificate and S is a holder of K and K is an attestation of D and K has course C.

# The conjunctive answer keeps the same dossier in the certificate and audit entry.
Find every S and K and D and A such that
S is a holder of K and K is an attestation of D and A is an auditEntry and A is an audit of D.
Find every S and C and M such that missing(S, C, M).
